ntil these five existed every one of the 17 vectors above carried a null transform, so a port that started folding the matrix here -- silently double-applying it wherever a caller applies the CTM itself -- moved no golden. Measured on this commit: both ports return the untransformed value for all five. Expectations are the twin vector's own `expected`, copied unchanged, so no new geometry is derived here -- which matters because the live reference implements no element bounds at all (workspace_interpreter duck-types `elem.bounds()` off the frozen port's geometry, doc_primitives.py line 85). THIS vector: translate(100,50) on the rect_bounds geometry; a port that folded it would return [105,60,100,50].","element":{"fill":null,"height":50.0,"locked":false,"opacity":1.0,"rx":0.0,"ry":0.0,"stroke":null,"transform":{"a":1.0,"b":0.0,"c":0.0,"d":1.0,"e":100.0,"f":50.0},"type":"rect","visibility":"preview","width":100.0,"x":5.0,"y":10.0},"expected":[5.0,10.0,100.0,50.0],"function":"bounds","name":"rect_transform_is_ignored"},{"_comment":"rotate(45) on the ellipse_bounds geometry. Non-commuting with axis-alignment, so it separates the ignore-contract from every folding rule at once: corner-mapping would give [-35.3553,35.3553,70.7107,70.7107] and a true rotated-ellipse bound [-25.4951,45.2156,50.9902,50.9902].","element":{"cx":50.0,"cy":50.0,"fill":null,"locked":false,"opacity":1.0,"rx":30.0,"ry":20.0,"stroke":null,"transform":{"a":0.7071067811865476,"b":0.7071067811865476,"c":-0.7071067811865476,"d":0.7071067811865476,"e":0.0,"f":0.0},"type":"ellipse","visibility":"preview"},"expected":[20.0,30.0,60.0,40.0],"function":"bounds","name":"ellipse_rotate_is_ignored"},{"_comment":"The path_cubic_tight_bounds curve under a general matrix (a=2 b=1 c=-0.5 d=1.5 e=7 f=-3), every entry live. Corner-mapping would give [3.25,-3,43.75,31.25] and the tight bounds of the TRANSFORMED curve [7,-3,40,23.923]; both differ from the answer, and from each other, in at least three components.","ele